<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="crafted-gear">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c8" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_mace_39.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Crafted &amp; Profession Gear for Fire Mages</span></h2>With Phase 3, we now get two new tailoring crafting options that are actually relevant:<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94278/falling-blossom-cowl">
<img alt="Falling Blossom Cowl" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helm_cloth_raidmage_m_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Falling Blossom Cowl</span></a> - This is a great option as an off-piece to use four-piece tier 15 set around assuming you are filling in those gaps with the Celestial versions of the set. At least until you get better items such as the best in slot chestpiece and/<wbr/>or the heroic tier 15 headpiece to replace it directly with.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94277/falling-blossom-treads">
<img alt="Falling Blossom Treads" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boot_cloth_raidmage_m_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Falling Blossom Treads</span></a> - is a straight upgrade from past phase options and with an additional socket it's great for both regular PVE content, and as Challenge Mode best in slot if you choose to do that later on, meaning your gold isn't wasted once you replace it in your raiding set.</div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="trinkets">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c8" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/creatureportrait_twilightshammer_dragonegg_01.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Pre-Raid Fire Mage Trinkets</span></h2>DPS trinkets tend to be very straightforward, and because the options available are limited, you can easily tell which one is better for you at the time. Of note, trinkets that deal direct damage should be used on cooldown as much as possible, unless they can be used during a boss mechanic that increases the boss' damage taken. Similarly, stat-increasing trinkets should either be used on cooldown or with burst phases.<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>For Fire Mages, two passive trinkets allow for higher top-end values if they both activate at the same time, meaning that you can then also use <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=126731/synapse-springs">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Synapse Springs</span></a> from your gloves followed by <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=108978/alter-time">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_mage_altertime.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Alter Time</span></a> to extend all three cooldowns, as well as any raid and class cooldowns you have active.<br/>
<br/>On the other hand, a combination of one active and one passive trinket allows for more consistent openings, since you can use the active trinket when the passive one procs. Although this has less top-end potential, it is more reliable because you are able to guarantee they're both active at the same time to combine with your own class cooldowns and <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=108978/alter-time">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_mage_altertime.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Alter Time</span></a>.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95772/cha-yes-essence-of-brilliance">
<img alt="Cha-Ye's Essence of Brilliance" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_mindsooth.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Cha-Ye's Essence of Brilliance</span></a> is the best pre-raid option for the trinket slots, it provides much needed Critical Strike which Fire Mage desperately needs early on - as well as a basic Intellect proc chance on Critical Strikes which fire can consitently get via its focus on said stat, as well as the Inferno Blast spell.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95669/wushoolays-final-choice">
<img alt="Wushoolay's Final Choice" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_chainlightning.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Wushoolay's Final Choice</span></a> is the second best trinket, and although lower item level than the new reputation trinket listed below, it performs significantly better due to better prioritization of stats since Fire Mage doesn't benefit as much from Haste as it once did in the past.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94510/volatile-talisman-of-the-shado-pan-assault">
<img alt="Volatile Talisman of the Shado-Pan Assault" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_hunter_posthaste.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Volatile Talisman of the Shado-Pan Assault</span></a> is still better than past phase trinkets, but due to its focus on Haste via its proc, it falls off in performance compared to the new raid trinkets' Celestial iterations.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79331/relic-of-yulon">
<img alt="Relic of Yu'lon" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_dragon.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Yu'lon</span></a> provides both static Intellect as well as a low-cooldown Intellect proc. Because of this it's a great early option if you manage to find one for relatively cheap while aiming for other slot upgrades first when you're farming Celestial dungeons.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86907/essence-of-terror">
<img alt="Essence of Terror" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_pvp_trinket.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Essence of Terror</span></a> is the LFR version of last phase's BiS trinket. It's of lower item level, but its static Intellect and great Haste proc work perfectly for Fire Mages. It got massively outscaled now but still a solid option if you've just hit level 90 and have some of the required currency for it on another character by chance.</div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="hit-expertise">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c8" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_marksmanship.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Reaching Hit and Expertise Cap for Fire Mages</span></h2>In Mists of Pandaria Classic, your Hit cap is 15%. Keep in mind that some abilities, such as the <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" data-contiguous="true" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/race_draenei_female.gif");'></span> Draenei racial Heroic Presence, will contribute to your overall Hit and/<wbr/>or Expertise needed.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="hit-expertise-rating">Hit &amp; Expertise Rating</h4>At 15% Hit, your spells will no longer miss raid bosses. It's also relevant to note that Expertise now counts as Hit and should be added together for the total of 15% to reach said cap.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="gemming">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c8" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_uncut_purple.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Gemming for Fire Mages</span></h2>As a Fire Mage, you'll aim for the highest Intellect possible, using <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76694/brilliant-primordial-ruby">
<img alt="Brilliant Primordial Ruby" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_red.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Brilliant Primordial Ruby</span></a>. Otherwise, with the secondary stats, we'll aim to get as much Critical Strike as possible, with <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76660/potent-vermilion-onyx">
<img alt="Potent Vermilion Onyx" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_orange.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Potent Vermilion Onyx</span></a>, and Hit, with <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76682/veiled-imperial-amethyst">
<img alt="Veiled Imperial Amethyst" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_purple.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Veiled Imperial Amethyst</span></a>.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="q9">Meta Gem</span>: <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95347/sinister-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Sinister Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_legendary_chimeraoffear.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sinister Primal Diamond</span></a> &gt; <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76885/burning-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Burning Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_metagem_cut.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Burning Primal Diamond</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c6">Red Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76694/brilliant-primordial-ruby">
<img alt="Brilliant Primordial Ruby" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_red.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Brilliant Primordial Ruby</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c7">Blue Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76682/veiled-imperial-amethyst">
<img alt="Veiled Imperial Amethyst" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_purple.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Veiled Imperial Amethyst</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c4">Yellow Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76660/potent-vermilion-onyx">
<img alt="Potent Vermilion Onyx" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_orange.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Potent Vermilion Onyx</span></a></div></li></ul>
<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<hr/>Our Fire Mage guides are always updated with the latest information from in-game experience, simulations, and logs; make sure to check our changelog to this page by clicking on <b>View Changelog</b> at the top of the page.<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
